  "id": "start-pitch-04-finding-c",
  "title": "Finding C",
  "summary": "Use the two black keys to find every C, then meet middle C.",
  "order": 2,
  "skills": [
    "pitch.keyboard.layout",
    "pitch.keyboard.find-notes",
    "pitch.high-low.hear"
  ],
  "prerequisites": [
    "start-pitch-03-twos-and-threes"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 6,
  "newTerms": [
    "middle-c"
  ],
  "steps": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "Press the three glowing keys, one after another. They share a name, and each sounds higher than the one before. Now look at where each key sits beside the black keys. What do you notice?",
      "exhibit": {
        "kind": "keyboard",
        "highlight": [
          "C3",
          "C4",
          "C5"
        ],
        "low": "C3",
        "high": "C5"
      }
    },
    "explore": {
      "text": "Find a group of 2 black keys. Press the white key on its left. Then do the same for every group of 2 you can see.",
      "instrument": "keyboard",
      "exhibit": {
        "kind": "keyboard",
        "highlight": [],
        "low": "C3",
        "high": "C5"
      },
      "goal": "Play the white key on the left of every group of 2 black keys."
    },
    "name": {
      "cards": [
        {
          "text": "That key is C. C always sits to the left of a group of 2 black keys. Find the twos, step left, and you have found C.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "C3",
              "C4",
              "C5"
            ],
            "low": "C3",
            "high": "C5"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Every C sounds like the same note at a different height. The C nearest the middle of the [[keyboard|keyboard]] is called [[middle-c|middle C]]. Pianists use it as a landmark.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "C4"
            ],
            "low": "C3",
            "high": "C5"
          }
        }
      ],
      "alternative": {
        "text": "Picture each group of 2 black keys as a pair of gateposts. C is the white key standing outside the left-hand gatepost. Spot a pair of gateposts, look to the left, and there is C.",
        "exhibit": {
          "kind": "keyboard",
          "highlight": [
            "C4"
          ],
          "low": "C4",
          "high": "B4"
        }
      }
    },
